            <ArticleTitle>Penile ulceration caused by a foreign body reaction in a crew member on board a cruise ship.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5603/IMH.2015.0008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A crew member had a foreign body implanted subcutaneously on his dorsum penis stealthily 6 years earlier by a fellow crew member without any medical training. He presented to the ship's medical centre after a week of pain, erythema and oedema over the foreign body, which was eventually removed by the patient, leaving behind a penile ulceration. He was treated conservatively initially with intravenous and then with oral antibiotics until complete secondary wound closure was achieved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
